### A concern about frame-driven tour vs timers
The tour timer runs every 16ms, incrementing its own frame counter. Other timers (input poll 16ms, data 1000ms) also run. Order within lv_timer_handler is by creation order. The tour timer is created last, so it runs after the input timer each tick. Injecting a key at frame N is processed by the input timer in the same tick (if input timer runs before tour this tick, it will be next tick +16ms). Negligible.

